---
code: syntax-malformed
when-fires: the parser hit a structurally malformed sh construct (a parse error); parsing continues fail-soft.
why: inv-no-throw: errors are data. PASSTHROUGH — the parser's description rides `detail`.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- syntax-malformed && mise run loom:promote -- syntax-malformed`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all syntax-malformed` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# the `for` loop never reaches its `done`
for pkg in nginx redis
do
  apt-get install -y "$pkg"

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
error[syntax-malformed]: sm expected `done` to close the loop
      [ book.sh:6:1
   6 | 
     | ^
